    {"rule": "cyrillic-latin transliteration", "detail": "Normalise both scripts to one internal key: ў->o', қ->q, ғ->g', ҳ->h, ш->sh, ч->ch, я->ya, ю->yu, ё->yo, ж->j, ц->ts, х->x, э->e."},
    {"rule": "mixed script", "detail": "Single utterances routinely mix scripts ('Korzinkadan 90 минг') because the keyboard was switched mid-sentence. Tokenise per-token, not per-utterance."},
    {"rule": "digit grouping", "detail": "'45 000', '45.000', '45,000', '45000' all mean 45000. A space or dot INSIDE a digit run is a thousands separator, not a decimal point — but '1.5 mln' IS a decimal. Disambiguate by whether a magnitude word follows."},
